#. de: Arbeit beginnt in: <if ($n1 > 0)> <num $n1> Std.</if><if ($n2 > 0)> <num $n2> Min.<else><if ($n1 > 0)><else> weniger als einer Minute</if></if> (<set-time $n3>am <num $day>.<num $month>. um <num $hour>:<num2 $min> Uhr)
#. fr: Début du prochain ouvrage dans <if ($n1 > 0)> <num $n1> heure<if ($n1 <= 1)><else>s</if></if><if ($n2 > 0)> <num $n2> minute<if ($n2 <= 1)><else>s</if></if><set-time $n3> (<num $day>.<num $month> à <num $hour>h<num2 $min>)
#. macro: <if ($n1 > 0)><num $n1>h</if> — shows the first branch when the condition holds, otherwise the branch after <else>; condition = number parameter 1 > 0 (condition: may be reworded, restructured, added, or dropped)
#. macro: <num $n1> — a number; value = number parameter 1 (game data: keep it; it may move or repeat)
#. macro: <if ($n2 == 0)><if ($n1 == 0)>less than 1m</if><else> <num $n2>m</if> — shows the first branch when the condition holds, otherwise the branch after <else>; condition = number parameter 2 == 0 (condition: may be reworded, restructured, added, or dropped)
#. macro: <if ($n1 == 0)>less than 1m</if> — shows the first branch when the condition holds, otherwise the branch after <else>; condition = number parameter 1 == 0 (condition: may be reworded, restructured, added, or dropped)
#. macro: <num $n2> — a number; value = number parameter 2 (game data: keep it; it may move or repeat)
#. macro: <set-time $n3> — sets the time placeholders ($hour, $day, …) to a Unix time; time = number parameter 3 (game data: keep it; it may move or repeat)
#. macro: <if ($gn77 == 3)><num $day>/<num $month><else><num $month>/<num $day></if> — shows the first branch when the condition holds, otherwise the branch after <else>; condition = global number 77 == 3 (condition: may be reworded, restructured, added, or dropped)
#. macro: <num $day> — a number; value = day of the month of the set time (game data: keep it; it may move or repeat)
#. macro: <num $month> — a number; value = month of the set time (game data: keep it; it may move or repeat)
#. macro: <num $hour> — a number; value = hour of the set time, 0–23 (game data: keep it; it may move or repeat)
#. macro: <num2 $min> — a number with at least two digits, such as 05; value = minutes of the set time (game data: keep it; it may move or repeat)
